WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.829
[SHAPE YOUR FUTURE]

00:00:17.246 --> 00:00:19.621
I want you to take this journey with me.

00:00:19.913 --> 00:00:21.496
Let's set the stage.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.288
It's a Sunday in Baltimore.

00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:25.621
There could be kids
in the park Druid Hill.

00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:28.079
They're watching dirt bike riders go pass,

00:00:28.079 --> 00:00:30.704
do tricks, pop wheelies, do stunts,

00:00:30.746 --> 00:00:31.996
they're zipping.

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:34.579
If you hear the engines revving,
smell the gasoline,

00:00:34.621 --> 00:00:37.121
you can see the joy
and excitement on their face.

00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:39.746
Someone’s probably learning
how to fix their dirt bike,

00:00:39.746 --> 00:00:42.496
because the parts
are way too expensive to buy.

00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:44.371
Then they can go to school.

00:00:44.829 --> 00:00:47.162
They can get a pop quiz
or a test from a teacher.

00:00:47.204 --> 00:00:49.621
You know the kind we all heard
and we've all hated.

00:00:49.621 --> 00:00:51.579
"A train that's leaving from New York,

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:53.037
goes to Cleveland,"

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:54.746
but they're here in Baltimore.

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:55.954
How does this relate?

00:00:55.996 --> 00:00:57.162
They don't get it.

00:00:57.162 --> 00:00:59.621
They fail the test
and now they can hate school.

00:00:59.662 --> 00:01:03.079
Then their world
can be turned upside down.

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:05.162
They can get on Facebook, on Instagram,

00:01:05.204 --> 00:01:06.829
get a call or a text.

00:01:06.871 --> 00:01:09.954
They can watch as their friend
can become a hashtag,

00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:12.579
a kid in the wrong place
at the wrong time.

00:01:12.912 --> 00:01:14.871
Lost to the streets, lost to the system

00:01:14.871 --> 00:01:16.663
or lost to gun violence.

00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:19.663
Or a kid that could be arrested
for a dirt bike.

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:20.913
Because in my city

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.704
it can be a misdemeanor
for possession of a dirt bike.

00:01:23.746 --> 00:01:26.788
This can be a likely story
for Black kids across the country.

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:30.663
In cities like Miami,
Cleveland, Atlanta, Philly,

00:01:30.704 --> 00:01:33.246
whatever place had
the dirt bike task force.

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:37.704
Now ask yourself if the thing
you use to relieve your stress,

00:01:37.746 --> 00:01:39.204
if it was demonized,

00:01:39.246 --> 00:01:40.496
would you still do it?

00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:42.579
If it was criminalized?

00:01:43.163 --> 00:01:44.579
The answer is yes.

00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:48.454
That's the reality for Black people
across the US right now.

00:01:48.454 --> 00:01:52.579
They’ve watched as we made room in cities
for skateboarders, for bicyclists

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.871
and any other sport.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:58.621
They can watch TV and see it on X Games,
the Olympics or ESPN.

00:01:58.621 --> 00:02:02.204
The style of riding can be seen
in ad campaigns and films.

00:02:02.204 --> 00:02:04.829
But in Baltimore, what do they
have to look forward to?

00:02:04.871 --> 00:02:06.496
What do riders get from all of it?

00:02:06.538 --> 00:02:08.954
No space, no outlet,

00:02:08.954 --> 00:02:10.621
just a typical narrative.

00:02:10.954 --> 00:02:13.163
Like I said, this is a common story.

00:02:13.204 --> 00:02:15.079
I was the kid in a park.

00:02:15.121 --> 00:02:17.663
I wanted to be just like
the big dirt-bike riders,

00:02:17.663 --> 00:02:18.996
but I hate to fall.

00:02:18.996 --> 00:02:21.788
Instead, I became like Bill Nye
The Science Guy.

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:24.913
I was doing all kinds of experiments,
blowing my eyebrows off,

00:02:24.954 --> 00:02:26.288
gluing people to the chair,

00:02:26.329 --> 00:02:29.246
and I may or may not have made
stink bombs at school.

00:02:29.913 --> 00:02:32.038
They would describe me as another bad kid.

00:02:32.038 --> 00:02:34.788
What they didn't see
was all my genius, my talent,

00:02:34.829 --> 00:02:36.496
my voice was not heard.

00:02:36.996 --> 00:02:40.288
Then I became that Black girl from
West Baltimore working in STEM.

00:02:40.704 --> 00:02:43.704
My first position, I was confused
for the secretary.

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:45.246
I was pissed.

00:02:46.121 --> 00:02:47.746
But it lit a fire in me.

00:02:47.788 --> 00:02:49.913
So I want to get more people
in the industry.

00:02:49.913 --> 00:02:51.954
And in 2013, that's what I started doing.

00:02:51.954 --> 00:02:54.204
Working in small groups
with kids and students,

00:02:54.204 --> 00:02:55.704
teaching them STEM activities.

00:02:55.746 --> 00:02:57.954
Then in 2014,

00:02:57.996 --> 00:03:00.704
I lost my little brother
to the prison system.

00:03:01.204 --> 00:03:04.996
In 2015, I lost all faith
in the system, period.

00:03:05.746 --> 00:03:08.704
The world watched the following
of Freddie Gray uprising

00:03:08.746 --> 00:03:10.204
as Baltimore burned.

00:03:10.246 --> 00:03:12.746
I wondered when were people
going to listen,

00:03:12.788 --> 00:03:14.246
where were the solutions?

00:03:14.246 --> 00:03:16.621
And where was the investment
into my community?

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:19.996
In 2016, I broke the system

00:03:19.996 --> 00:03:23.121
and became the founder and CEO of B-360,

00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:24.829
carving out a new lane.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.829
I went back to my experience in the park.

00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:28.954
I thought about the kids
fixing their bikes.

00:03:28.954 --> 00:03:31.454
Those are skills people use
to pay the bills,

00:03:31.496 --> 00:03:33.871
just like mechanics
and mechanical engineers.

00:03:33.871 --> 00:03:35.663
We leaned into STEM.

00:03:35.663 --> 00:03:37.454
S -- Science.

00:03:37.496 --> 00:03:39.788
The science behind
popping the best wheelie,

00:03:39.829 --> 00:03:41.788
pulling your dirt bike at twelve o'clock

00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:42.996
is a physics equation.

00:03:42.996 --> 00:03:44.746
T -- Technology.

00:03:44.788 --> 00:03:47.788
The technology needed to get
the best radial tires

00:03:47.788 --> 00:03:49.871
so you don't have frictional asphalt.

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:51.496
E -- Engineering.

00:03:51.538 --> 00:03:54.121
The engineering needed
to fix or peg a dirt bike,

00:03:54.163 --> 00:03:56.746
but to also get the best "mac mac" noise.

00:03:56.746 --> 00:03:58.788
M -- Mathematics.

00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:01.621
The math needed for the gas to oil ratio

00:04:01.663 --> 00:04:03.954
so your dirt bike does not explode.

00:04:03.996 --> 00:04:05.621
Then I took it a step further.

00:04:05.621 --> 00:04:07.079
I thought about the riders.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:09.913
I knew the only way
to have program and solutions

00:04:09.913 --> 00:04:11.829
was to have them at the table.

00:04:11.871 --> 00:04:14.704
Because the people closest
to the problem are the solution.

00:04:14.996 --> 00:04:16.329
I thought about Mike.

00:04:16.371 --> 00:04:18.788
Since he was six,
he's been riding dirt bikes.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:20.954
When he was 17, graduating high school,

00:04:20.954 --> 00:04:22.704
he didn't know what he wanted to do,

00:04:22.746 --> 00:04:25.454
but he knew he loved
everything about dirt bikes.

00:04:25.454 --> 00:04:27.454
He started working with us in B-360,

00:04:27.496 --> 00:04:29.163
he's helped us educate kids,

00:04:29.204 --> 00:04:30.621
train dirt bike riders,

00:04:30.663 --> 00:04:32.996
and at 21 he's our lead instructor.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.454
He's created events,

00:04:34.454 --> 00:04:35.996
he's traveled across the country

00:04:36.038 --> 00:04:38.829
and he really represents
the best of B-360.

00:04:38.871 --> 00:04:40.163
At the core of our work

00:04:40.204 --> 00:04:43.329
is constantly thinking
about what people like Mike want.

00:04:43.371 --> 00:04:45.204
For Mike, he wants a space.

00:04:45.496 --> 00:04:48.621
A space where he can keep working
with students on our curriculum,

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.788
a space where he can keep
training more riders

00:04:50.829 --> 00:04:52.413
and growing their skill sets,

00:04:52.454 --> 00:04:55.079
a space where he no longer has to escape,

00:04:55.079 --> 00:04:57.454
but he has something
in his own city for him.

00:04:57.954 --> 00:05:00.413
With your support
and the support of more cities,

00:05:00.454 --> 00:05:02.204
we can make this a reality.

00:05:02.246 --> 00:05:03.996
Since 2017,

00:05:04.038 --> 00:05:09.246
we've saved the city of Baltimore
about 233 million dollars

00:05:09.288 --> 00:05:12.204
by doing programing
for over 7,000 students.

00:05:12.246 --> 00:05:15.204
We've saved the city of Baltimore
one million dollars

00:05:15.246 --> 00:05:18.913
by growing work force and opportunities
for people just like Mike.

00:05:19.454 --> 00:05:21.954
That's less people
that could possibly go to jail,

00:05:21.996 --> 00:05:25.538
less money spent on dollars
and cents of incarceration

00:05:25.579 --> 00:05:28.996
and more money going back
into our Black communities, our leaders,

00:05:29.038 --> 00:05:30.913
our culture and our voices.

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:32.913
We don't need your black squares,

00:05:32.954 --> 00:05:34.954
we don't need your campaigns,

00:05:34.996 --> 00:05:38.288
but what we do need
is your dollars and cents behind us

00:05:38.329 --> 00:05:39.829
to make real change.

00:05:39.829 --> 00:05:41.788
We need more people like you in cities

00:05:41.829 --> 00:05:45.288
to believe in investing in us
and our model of growing the people.

00:05:45.288 --> 00:05:46.871
What will you choose to be?

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.413
An ally?

00:05:48.746 --> 00:05:49.913
Be an impact?

00:05:50.246 --> 00:05:51.871
Be the revolution?

00:05:51.871 --> 00:05:53.413
B-360.

00:05:54.121 --> 00:05:55.246
Thank you.

